# Vulnerability details

## Explanation
The [`EthenaMinting.sol#_setMaxMintPerBlock()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-10-ethena/blob/main/contracts/EthenaMinting.sol#L436-L440) function is responsible for `setting the maximum limit for minting USDe tokens in a single block`.

```jsx
  function setMaxMintPerBlock(uint256 _maxMintPerBlock) external onlyRole(DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE) {
    _setMaxMintPerBlock(_maxMintPerBlock);
  }

  function _setMaxMintPerBlock(uint256 _maxMintPerBlock) internal {
    uint256 oldMaxMintPerBlock = maxMintPerBlock;
    maxMintPerBlock = _maxMintPerBlock;
    emit MaxMintPerBlockChanged(oldMaxMintPerBlock, maxMintPerBlock);
  }
```

## Proof of Concept

Maybe the most discussed vulnerability in the protocol is the potential malicious user who can `to mint any amount of USDe for any amount of collateral` (effectively to drain the EthenaMinting contract). But the `Ethena` mitigate this problem...
> "Our solution is to enforce an on chain mint and redeem limitation of 100k USDe per block" 
**from the contest [page/documentation](https://code4rena.com/contests/2023-10-ethena-labs#top:~:text=Our%20solution%20is,affect%20our%20operations.)** 

However this isn't actually implemented in the code as we can see in `_setMaxRedeemPerBlock()` function ([EthenaMinting contract](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-10-ethena/blob/main/contracts/EthenaMinting.sol)).
```jsx
  function _setMaxRedeemPerBlock(uint256 _maxRedeemPerBlock) internal {
    uint256 oldMaxRedeemPerBlock = maxRedeemPerBlock;
    maxRedeemPerBlock = _maxRedeemPerBlock;
    emit MaxRedeemPerBlockChanged(oldMaxRedeemPerBlock, maxRedeemPerBlock);
  }
```


As a result, this vulnerability `opens` the most discussed known attack vector in the protocol (`malicious minter who can to mint any amount of USDe for any amount of collateral`).

