# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Attackers could instantly withdraw all rewards meant to be vested over time, disrupting the incentive structure and sustainability of the protocol.
The severity is high. This is a critical vulnerability that undermines a core mechanism of the contract. Overall this is a critical issue since it allows the core vesting logic to be circumvented. It violates the intended reward distribution principles of the protocol 
The vesting period is important for aligning incentives over time. Bypassing it too easily can destabilize the system. 

