# Vulnerability details

## Impact
***Fund loss dues to lack of ensuring that the owner is the msg.sender for every 8 hours without the consent of the owner. Since there is no check to ensure that the owner is the same and msg.sender that means an attacker can use this function to withdraw shares on behalf of the owner if they know their addresses. Moreover, an attacker front-runs legitimate transactions, quickly executing this function every 8 hours before the right owner does, potentially draining the shares of the owner.***

## Proof of Concept
```
  function cooldownShares(uint256 shares, address owner) external ensureCooldownOn returns (uint256) {
    if (shares > maxRedeem(owner)) revert ExcessiveRedeemAmount();

    uint256 assets = previewRedeem(shares);

    cooldowns[owner].cooldownEnd = uint104(block.timestamp) + cooldownDuration;
    cooldowns[owner].underlyingAmount += assets;

    _withdraw(_msgSender(), address(silo), owner, assets, shares);

    return assets;
  }
```
***Let's say the attacker comes online to check different addresses on the explorer and he finds some with funds in them, he selects them and then creates a malicious contract to exploit the stakedUsdeV2 since the `cooldownShares` function can be called by anyone for every 8 hours. The attacker waits for the exact time to run his malicious contract on that function. His malicious contract would contain the address of the legitimate user and he would specify his owner address(attacker's own) then he would wait for Alice to initiate a cooldown.***
```
