# Vulnerability details

## Impact
In this contract, the ensureCooldownOff modifier performs a revert if the cooldownDuration is not equal to zero, so in this case ensureCooldownOff will always trigger the revert so that the withdraw and redeem methods will never succeed. This means that the user will not be able to retrieve their assets because these two methods are permanently disabled.

## Proof of Concept
Set cooldownDuration 14~90 days
```solidity
  function setCooldownDuration(uint24 duration) external onlyRole(DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE) {
    if (duration > MAX_COOLDOWN_DURATION) {
      revert InvalidCooldown();
    }

    uint24 previousDuration = cooldownDuration;
    cooldownDuration = duration;
    emit CooldownDurationUpdated(previousDuration, cooldownDuration);
  }
```
`cooldownDuration` is not 0, which causes `modifier ensureCooldownOff()` to always return to `revert`.

The `withdraw` and `redeem` functions are disabled because they are modified by `ensureCooldownOff`.
```
  function withdraw(uint256 assets, address receiver, address owner)
    public
    virtual
    override
    ensureCooldownOff
    returns (uint256)
  {
    return super.withdraw(assets, receiver, owner);
  }
  function redeem(uint256 shares, address receiver, address owner)
    public
    virtual
    override
    ensureCooldownOff
    returns (uint256)
  {
    return super.redeem(shares, receiver, owner);
  }
```

## Tools Used
Manual review
## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Rewrite the `modifier` to fix this logic error.

```solidity
modifier onlyAfterCooldown(address owner) {
    if (cooldowns[owner].cooldownEnd != 0 && block.timestamp < cooldowns[owner].cooldownEnd) {
        revert InvalidCooldown();
    }
    _;
}

