EthenaMinting.mint function is used to mint stable coin from asset and transfer to custodian address per defined ratio via `_transferCollateral` internal function.
mint function includes various checks before actual transfer of collateral like first it check if the order type is mint otherwise it will throw an error next it calls `verifyOrder` function which assert validity of signed order and later on it make a call to `verifyRoute` which checks certain functionalities related to route address, route ratio and at last it calls `_deduplicateOrder`, which revert with an duplicate order error in case the order and nonce used again and finally it make a call to `_transferCollateral` function that transfer supported asset to array of custody addresses per defined ratio and where the actual vulnerability lies.

